      "about": "Formal designations, as surveys write them. Planets take Roman numerals by orbit (the default) and their moons letters. Stars are SX and a running number, or SX J and their sky position; the components of a multiple star are A, B, C; surface features take the IAU's Latin descriptor terms with the world's name and a number. Every designation follows its parent's name when that is renamed. Sources: IAU naming rules, Hessman et al. 2010 (arXiv:1012.0707), the Washington Multiplicity Catalog, and the USGS and IAU Gazetteer of Planetary Nomenclature (docs/citations/naming.md).",
